# Brackish Blunder {1}{U}: "Return target creature to its owner's hand. If it was tapped, create a Map token." Bot1's Memnite attacks
# on turn 3 (an attacker taps, so it is tapped as the spell resolves) while Bot2's Ornithopter stays home untapped: Blunder targeting
# the Memnite is a choice between the two creatures (it can target either). The tapped Memnite returns to its owner's hand and Bot1
# creates a Map token (CR 400.3, 608.2c); Bot2's untapped Ornithopter is untouched and Bot2 gets nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Memnite
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Brackish Blunder
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Brackish Blunder.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Map Token; Mox Jet; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Memnite
Bot1.Graveyard = Brackish Blunder
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
